        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">The Sole TT8 is Sole’s heaviest, most capable treadmill</strong>: a 4.0 HP
            motor, a 22 by 60-inch deck, decline, a 400 lb rating and a lifetime frame and motor
            warranty, on a non-folding frame. It was sold out on Sole’s US store on 5 November 2026,
            and the current version’s warranty is shorter than older reviews describe.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If you can wait, wait for Sole’s $2,899.99 list price. If you cannot, the
            <a href="/sole-f85-treadmill/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">Sole F85</a>
            gives you the same deck and screen for $700 less without decline, and the NordicTrack X16
            gives you more decline for more money.
          </p>
